    <title>This Is Lorelei – The Singer in My Band</title>
    <link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/this-is-lorelei-the-singer-in-my-band/</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="true">https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/this-is-lorelei-the-singer-in-my-band/</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 04:03:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <enclosure url="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6a3aa2af3d85cbbe413a9dc2/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/This%20Is%20Lorelei%20-%20The%20Singer%20in%20My%20Band%20_%20Album%20Art%20(1).jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/>
    <description><![CDATA[<p>On his first album for Matador, Nate Amos trades the magpie charm of his past solo work for a warm, twangy, and tightly constructed approach. It’s the sound of a songwriter sketching out his own gospel.</p>
<img src="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6a3aa2af3d85cbbe413a9dc2/16:9/w_1280,c_limit/This%20Is%20Lorelei%20-%20The%20Singer%20in%20My%20Band%20_%20Album%20Art%20(1).jpg" alt="The Singer in My Band cover"/>
